{"abstract":"Guarded Interaction Trees are a structure and a fully formalized framework for representing higher-order computations with higher-order effects in Coq. We present an extension of Guarded Interaction Trees to support formal reasoning about context-dependent effects. That is, effects whose behaviors depend on the evaluation context, e.g., call/cc, shift and reset. Using and reasoning about such effects is challenging since certain compositionality principles no longer hold in the presence of such effects. For example, the so-called “bind rule” in modern program logics (which allows one to reason modularly about a term inside a context) is no longer valid. The goal of our extension is to support representation and reasoning about context-dependent effects in the most painless way possible. To that end, our extension is conservative: the reasoning principles (and the Coq implementation) for context-independent effects remain the same. We show that our implementation of context-dependent effects is viable and powerful. We use it to give direct-style denotational semantics for higher-order programming languages with call/cc and with delimited continuations. We extend the program logic for Guarded Interaction Trees to account for context-dependent effects, and we use the program logic to prove that the denotational semantics is adequate with respect to the operational semantics. This is achieved by constructing logical relations between syntax and semantics inside the program logic. Additionally, we retain the ability to combine multiple effects in a modular way, which we demonstrate by showing type soundness for safe interoperability of a programming language with delimited continuations and a programming language with higher-order store.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Stepanenko, Sergei","Nardino, Emma","Frumin, Dan","Timany, Amin","Birkedal, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816646"],"event":{"end":"2025-05-08","place":"Hamilton, ca","start":"2025-05-03","title":"34th European Symposium on Programming, ESOP 2025, which was held as part of the International Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stepanenko, Sergei"],"country":["France","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Groningen","École Normale Supérieure de Lyon"],"keyword":["Continuations","Coq","Denotational Semantics","Iris","Logical Relations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"context dependent effects in guarded interaction trees","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-91121-7_12","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816646","identifier":[{"id":"105004788519","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-caad8da5-d798-4b96-aaef-dd718ae23049"],"keyword":["Coq","Iris","continuations","control flow operators","delimited continuations","denotational semantics","logical relations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-83DA7F09ED2B293165BDA42CED4BC68F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-91121-7_12","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"école normale supérieure de lyon","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"École Normale Supérieure de Lyon","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sergei","key":"stepanenkopau","last":"Stepanenko","locid":"0bdc2e30-d814-42f0-a48d-12db7f01673e","name":"Stepanenko, Sergei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma","key":"nardinopau","last":"Nardino","name":"Nardino, Emma","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"fruminpau","last":"Frumin","name":"Frumin, Dan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amin","key":"timanypau","last":"Timany","locid":"e651b5c3-4642-4bcd-8108-224aa2ecfc08","name":"Timany, Amin","orcid":"0000-0002-2237-851X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","locid":"bd012524-7d01-45f4-9bbd-8f8273bf14c7","name":"Birkedal, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1320-0098","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Viktor","key":"vafeiadispedh","last":"Vafeiadis","name":"Vafeiadis, Viktor","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-91121-7_12","isbn":["9783031911200"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"286-313","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Programming Languages and Systems - 34th European Symposium on Programming, ESOP 2025, Held as Part of the International Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2025, Proceedings","volume":"Part II"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004788519"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-caad8da5-d798-4b96-aaef-dd718ae23049"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Context-Dependent Effects in Guarded Interaction Trees","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816646","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Constructing solutions to recursive domain equations is a well-known, important problem in the study of programs and programming languages. Mathematically speaking, the problem is finding a fixed point (up to isomorphism) of a suitable functor over a suitable category. A particularly useful instance, inspired by the step-indexing technique, is where the functor is over (a subcategory of) the category of presheaves over the ordinal ω and the functors are locally-contractive, also known as guarded functors. This corresponds to step-indexing over natural numbers. However, for certain problems, e.g., when dealing with infinite non-determinism, one needs to employ trans-finite step-indexing, i.e., consider presheaf categories over higher ordinals. Prior work on trans-finite step-indexing either only considers a very narrow class of functors over a particularly restricted subcategory of presheaves over higher ordinals, or treats the problem very generally working with sheaves over an arbitrary complete Heyting algebra with a well-founded basis. In this paper we present a solution to the guarded domain equations problem over all guarded functors over the category of presheaves over ordinal numbers, as well as its mechanization in the Rocq Prover. As the categories of sheaves and presheaves over ordinals are equivalent, our main contribution is simplifying prior work from the setting of the category of sheaves to the setting of the category of presheaves and mechanizing it - presheaves are more amenable to mechanization in a proof assistant.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stepanenko, Sergei","Timany, Amin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-825805"],"event":{"end":"2025-07-20","place":"Birmingham, gb","start":"2025-07-14","title":"10th International Conference on Formal Structures for Computation and Deduction, FSCD 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Stepanenko, Sergei","Timany, Amin"],"keyword":["Category theory","Fixed points","Ordinals"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"solving guarded domain equations in presheaves over ordinals and mechanizing it","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2025.33","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-825805","identifier":[{"id":"105010680374","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-92105d5d-ab0a-48ef-adeb-f71d4fe24af4"],"keyword":["Category Theory","Domain Equations","Fixed Points","Guarded Fixed Points","Ordinals","Presheaves","Rocq"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A1FBB2B81431533DD331432352876192"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2025.33","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sergei","key":"stepanenkopau","last":"Stepanenko","locid":"0bdc2e30-d814-42f0-a48d-12db7f01673e","name":"Stepanenko, Sergei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amin","key":"timanypau","last":"Timany","locid":"e651b5c3-4642-4bcd-8108-224aa2ecfc08","name":"Timany, Amin","orcid":"0000-0002-2237-851X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maribel","key":"fernandezpedh","last":"Fernandez","name":"Fernandez, Maribel","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.fscd.2025.33","eisbn":["9783959773744"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"10th International Conference on Formal Structures for Computation and Deduction, FSCD 2025"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010680374"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-92105d5d-ab0a-48ef-adeb-f71d4fe24af4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Solving Guarded Domain Equations in Presheaves over Ordinals and Mechanizing It","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-825805","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This paper considers direct encodings of generalized algebraic data types (GADTs) in a minimal suitable lambda-calculus. To this end, we develop an extension of System Fω with recursive types and internalized type equalities with injective constant type constructors. We show how GADTs and associated pattern-matching constructs can be directly expressed in the calculus, thus showing that it may be treated as a highly idealized modern functional programming language. We prove that the internalized type equalities in conjunction with injectivity rules increase the expressive power of the calculus by establishing a non-macro-expressibility result in Fω, and prove the system type-sound via a syntactic argument. Finally, we build two relational models of our calculus: a simple, unary model that illustrates a novel, two-stage interpretation technique, necessary to account for the equational constraints; and a more sophisticated, binary model that relaxes the construction to allow, for the first time, formal reasoning about data-abstraction in a calculus equipped with GADTs.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sieczkowski, Filip","Stepanenko, Sergei","Sterling, Jonathan","Birkedal, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-726853"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Heriot-Watt University","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Logical Relations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the essence of generalized algebraic data types","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3632866","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-726853","identifier":[{"id":"85182274158","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-21ce707f-e751-4cab-ab4c-9caa715fd7df"],"keyword":["Generalized Algebraic Data Types","Logical Relations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A7B3102CD1C00CA66D70FBEEE3D6DA8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3632866","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"heriot watt university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Heriot-Watt University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Filip","key":"sieczkowskipau","last":"Sieczkowski","name":"Sieczkowski, Filip","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sergei","key":"stepanenkopau","last":"Stepanenko","locid":"0bdc2e30-d814-42f0-a48d-12db7f01673e","name":"Stepanenko, Sergei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan","key":"sterlingpau","last":"Sterling","name":"Sterling, Jonathan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","locid":"bd012524-7d01-45f4-9bbd-8f8273bf14c7","name":"Birkedal, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1320-0098","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3632866","issn":["24751421"],"issue":"POPL","journal":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","pages":"695-723","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182274158"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-21ce707f-e751-4cab-ab4c-9caa715fd7df"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Essence of Generalized Algebraic Data Types","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-726853","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Thin hypervisors make it possible to isolate key security components like keychains, fingerprint readers, and digital wallets from the easily-compromised operating system. To work together, virtual machines running on top of the hypervisor can make hypercalls to the hypervisor to share pages between each other in a controlled way. However, the design of such hypercall ABIs remains a delicate balancing task between conflicting needs for expressivity, performance, and security. In particular, it raises the question of what makes the specification of a hypervisor, and of its hypercall ABIs, good enough for the virtual machines. In this paper, we validate the expressivity and security of the design of the hypercall ABIs of Arm's FF-A. We formalise a substantial fragment of FF-A as a machine with a simplified ISA in which hypercalls are steps of the machine. We then develop VMSL, a novel separation logic, which we prove sound with respect to the machine execution model, and use it to reason modularly about virtual machines which communicate through the hypercall ABIs, demonstrating the hypercall ABIs' expressivity. Moreover, we use the logic to prove robust safety of communicating virtual machines, that is, the guarantee that even if some of the virtual machines are compromised and execute unknown code, they cannot break the safety properties of other virtual machines running known code. This demonstrates the intended security guarantees of the hypercall ABIs. All the results in the paper have been formalised in Coq using the Iris framework.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Liu, Zongyuan","Stepanenko, Sergei","Pichon-Pharabod, Jean","Timany, Amin","Askarov, Aslan","Birkedal, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-687945"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Iris","Logical Relation","Separation logic","robust safety"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vmsl a separation logic for mechanised robust safety of virtual machines communicating above ff a","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3591279","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-687945","identifier":[{"id":"85161967397","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-86004023-0ec2-49c0-9f8e-e521c80a4446"],"keyword":["FF-A","Iris","hypercall","logical relation","robust safety","separation logic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9650AF7D237BD6622B0A70C5D96EBE7D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/420153176/3591279.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3591279","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zongyuan","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"000f0860-6adc-4670-af97-1b82cbe1e1c1","name":"Liu, Zongyuan","orcid":"0000-0001-9652-4869","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sergei","key":"stepanenkopau","last":"Stepanenko","locid":"0bdc2e30-d814-42f0-a48d-12db7f01673e","name":"Stepanenko, Sergei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jean","key":"pichonpharabodpau","last":"Pichon-Pharabod","locid":"7705419e-fa64-4319-b0c1-da0f61ad128c","name":"Pichon-Pharabod, Jean","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amin","key":"timanypau","last":"Timany","locid":"e651b5c3-4642-4bcd-8108-224aa2ecfc08","name":"Timany, Amin","orcid":"0000-0002-2237-851X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aslan","key":"askarovpau","last":"Askarov","locid":"bf41dbdb-03c3-4ffd-85aa-cafd000e6384","name":"Askarov, Aslan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"birkedalpau","last":"Birkedal","locid":"bd012524-7d01-45f4-9bbd-8f8273bf14c7","name":"Birkedal, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1320-0098","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3591279","issn":["24751421"],"journal":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","pages":"1438-1462","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161967397"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-86004023-0ec2-49c0-9f8e-e521c80a4446"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"VMSL : A Separation Logic for Mechanised Robust Safety of Virtual Machines Communicating above FF-A","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-687945","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
